pletion. Rejection responses retry earlier suffix; compaction selects snapshot for active peers.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-replicate\",\n        \"B-persist\",\n        \"B-apply\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-committed\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-core-commit\",\n        \"M-core-dispatch\",\n        \"M-log-rules\",\n        \"M-engine-order\",\n        \"M-node-consume\",\n        \"M-rsm-apply\",\n        \"M-replicate-send\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Election timers initiate campaign only for eligible full voters without committed-but-unapplied work. New term resets transient votes/progress/read confirmations; vote granting checks log freshness and prior vote, and candidate forms authority from deduplicated quorum replies. Higher-term protocol messages normally cause stepdown, with check-quorum vote suppression exception; lower terms are ignored. Same-term leader messages demote candidates. Quorum checks, removal and transfer govern loss/change of leadership. Transfer waits for target catchup and triggers target election via TimeoutNow, while blocking proposals until completion or timeout.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-membership\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-committed\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-core-commit\",\n        \"M-core-dispatch\",\n        \"M-response-routing\",\n        \"M-timers\",\n        \"M-transfer\",\n        \"M-quorum-check\",\n        \"M-candidate-stepdown\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Terms qualify newly counted support, but established committed history survives authority reset and constrains future logs and votes. Membership becomes active through RSM application; campaign defers when applied state lags commit, so a new leader does not simply form using its old unapplied membership. New leader reconstructs pending config status and commits a current-term no-op before multi-voter ReadIndex admission. Pending read contexts are reset with authority; within one leader context, voter heartbeat confirmation releases queue prefixes for local readiness or forwarded replies, and clients require exact context plus applied index. Old network responses are term-filtered and unknown responders rejected; pending client work may independently drop or timeout.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-read-confirm\",\n        \"B-read-route\",\n        \"B-client-read\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-committed\",\n        \"F-read-release\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-core-commit\",\n        \"M-core-dispatch\",\n        \"M-peer\",\n        \"M-heartbeat-producer\",\n        \"M-read-reply\",\n        \"M-read-client\",\n        \"M-node-callbacks\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Forwarded replies use triggering confirmation context for every released queue status; exact correlation under overlapping reads remains unresolved.\",\n      \"Disk/concurrent state machine crash/recovery, storage implementations, session deduplication and membership-change message interleavings remain deeper variants.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation, authority changes, stale-work handling and their persistence/membership/application connections have been traced. Local read-response correlation and deeper fault variants remain questions, not unexplained core ownership.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"1f8f0894ea604a0e95f0f52e012a54ec\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"1f8f0894ea604a0e95f0f52e012a54ec\"\n        }\n   