,\n        \"ctx\":assuranceContext(ctx), \"term\":r.term, \"captured_index\":s.index,\n        \"pending_count\":len(r.readIndex.queue),\n    })\n    return probes\n}\n\nfunc TestAssuranceForwardedReadContexts(t *testing.T) {\n    for _, overlap := range []bool{false,true} {\n        scenario := \"serial\"\n        if overlap { scenario=\"overlap\" }\n        t.Run(scenario, func(t *testing.T) {\n            n := assuranceNewReadNetwork(t, scenario)\n            first := n.admit(2, pb.SystemCtx{Low:101,High:1001})\n            if !overlap { n.drain(first) }\n            second := n.admit(3, pb.SystemCtx{Low:202,High:2002})\n            // Deliver the later request'\"'s probes and all their descendants\n            // before delivering any of the earlier request's held probes.\n            // No message is fabricated, rewritten, or dropped.\n            n.drain(second)\n            if overlap { n.drain(first) }\n            r := n.nodes[1].peer.raft\n            assuranceReadEvent(map[string]interface{}{\n                \\\"event\\\":\\\"drained\\\", \\\"scenario\\\":scenario, \\\"term\\\":r.term,\n                \\\"pending_count\\\":len(r.readIndex.queue), \\\"result_count\\\":n.resultCount,\n                \\\"steps\\\":n.steps,\n            })\n        })\n    }\n}\nGO\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json')); candidate=r['candidates'][0]\nq=candidate['question'].copy()\nq['unknowns']=['Actual same-history response/readiness contexts under a legal overlap remain unmeasured.']\nq['disposition']='ready_for_check'\nsources=[dict(id='M-read-prefix-test',file='internal/raft/readindex_test.go',start_line=125,end_line=162,kind='test_expectation'),dict(id='M-test-logdb',file='internal/raft/logdb_test.go',start_line=24,end_line=156,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-peer-launch',file='internal/raft/peer.go',start_line=70,end_line=104,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-peer-bootstrap',file='internal/raft/peer.go',start_line=405,end_line=470,kind='code_observation')]\nclaimid='C-forwarded-context';binding='BD-forwarded-context'\nexpect=['M-read-prefix-test','M-read-receiver-test','M-read-api']\nimpl=['M-read-queue','M-read-reply','M-follower-read','M-read-client','M-node-read-entry','M-peer']\nderivation='M-read-prefix-test explicitly expects a prefix release to retain the individual ctx/from of each earlier status even when its index is advanced. M-read-receiver-test expects received Hint/HintHigh to become the readiness SystemCtx. M-read-api makes readiness completion belong to the returned operation, while M-read-client and M-node-read-entry implement that association with an exact SystemCtx batch key. Together these ground preservation of the original admitted context when routing a released status to its origin. They do not require immediate success for every admitted read or preservation of its old index. The suspect sender implementation is the subject of comparison, not the source of the expected output.'\nclaim=dict(id=claimid,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='Within a stable leader term and fixed full-voter membership, when qualified confirmation releases a queued forwarded ReadIndex status and the implementation routes its response to the originating follower, the readiness context exported at that follower must equal the context admitted for that status. Coalescing may raise the read index, but must not substitute another request context.',source_ids=impl+expect,scope=dict(description='Per-status correlation through completed forwarded-read response routing in a crash-free three-full-voter cluster with current-term committed history and distinct request contexts.',assumptions=['Each originating follower has one outstanding operation in the checked history, allowing independent correlation by origin.', 'All actual protocol messages are delivered without mutation; the overlap delays earlier heartbeat probes until later-context confirmation has completed.', 'Peer caller persists each update before message delivery and applies bootstrap configuration/no-op entries in order.'],excluded=['No claim of a client API deadline, infinite stall, state-machine read linearizability violation, or crash durability failure.', 'No membership changes, observer/witness roles, snapshots, or term changes during the read phase.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=impl,expectation_ids=expect,binding_ids=[binding],derivation=derivation,applicability='Only actually exported readiness from qualified queued forwarded-read release; comparison retains coalesced index semantics and uses independent origin identity.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['An implementation could legally coalesce read indices; that does not explain replacing the exact context key required by the consumer.','A permitted drop or timeout would not establish a context mismatch; missing result remains incomplete.']))\nbind=dict(id=binding,material_id='M-read-reply',symbol='raft.handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation',start_line=1771,end_line=1790,description='Routes statuses released by readIndex.confirm either to local readiness with s.ctx or a remote ReadIndexResp carrying m.Hint/m.HintHigh.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claimid,source_ids=impl+expect,rationale=derivation)])\nlegalsources=['M-peer-launch','M-peer-bootstrap','M-test-logdb','M-peer','M-engine-order','M-free-order','M-core-dispatch','M-core-commit','M-timers','M-heartbeat-producer','M-read-queue','M-follower-read','M-read-reply','M-node-read-entry','M-read-prefix-test','M-read-receiver-test']\nlegality=dict(source_ids=legalsources,expectation_ids=['M-read-prefix-test','M-read-receiver-test'],binding_ids=[binding],derivation='Harness uses actual Launch with identical bootstrap membership on three Peers, the existing in-memory TestLogDB adapter, and actual Tick-triggered election on node 1. Every returned Update is appended/saved before any message is deliverable, then committed; committed bootstrap config entries are passed to ApplyConfigChange and the no-op is consumed in order, with NotifyRaftLastApplied reporting that work. This is a crash-free adapter, not a disk durability test. During the fixed-membership read phase, only actual Peer.ReadIndex, produced messages via Peer.Handle, and GetUpdate/Commit are used. ReadIndex calls from nodes 2 and 3 produce distinct contexts and are forwarded by actual followers; later heartbeat probes are delivered and fully drained before earlier held probes. Delaying an older probe across a newer one is a normal asynchronous network schedule and no helper serializes the two reads. All messages are eventually delivered unchanged. The setup explicitly verifies elected role, shared term/leader, current-term committed no-op and synchronized applied prefix. There is no private-state mutation, mocked handler, or fabricated response. Private pending state is read solely to record admission and final queue state.',applicability='Fixed membership, no crashes or compaction, only bootstrap configuration and empty application entry, one operation per originating follower per scenario.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Serial fresh-network control drains each read before admitting the next; overlap differs only in probe delivery order.'])\nmonitor_ground=dict(source_ids=impl,expectation_ids=expect,binding_ids=[binding],derivation=derivation+' Results read ReadyToReads directly from each receiving Peer Update before Commit clears the buffer. scenario plus receiving origin identify the operation independently of ctx. read_admitted.ctx records the originating Peer input after actual leader admission; read_result.ctx is the exported observed context. Wire response events preserve the intermediate route but are diagnostics, not substitutes for the receiver observation.',applicability='Every exported result at the two originating followers is retained; no result is filtered by expected context or index. Missing or ambiguous results remain incomplete.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[])\nplan=dict(description='Compare sequential and overlapping reads in fresh three-Peer networks. Real bootstrap, Tick election and committed no-op precede both scenarios. In overlap, nodes 2 and 3 each submit a distinct ReadIndex; node 3 probes confirm first, releasing the queued prefix. Deliver every generated response and then every held earlier probe. Compare each receiving ReadyToRead context with that originating operation input, using scenario/origin rather than ctx as identity. Wire messages and drained queue counts are diagnostics. This fixes inputs before execution and does not treat finite waiting as a liveness oracle.',claim_id=claimid,binding_ids=[binding],harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='TestAssuranceForwardedReadContexts in package raft, exercising actual Peer producer/consumer paths with existing TestLogDB as a crash-free persistence adapter.',semantic_changes=['No target implementation changes.', 'Deterministic in-process transport delivers messages, deferring earlier probes only in overlap.', 'Application adapter consumes only bootstrap membership entries and the election no-op; no user state-machine result is simulated.', 'Read-only private fields establish setup/admission and diagnostics; decisive observations use Peer.GetUpdate ReadyToReads.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='admitted',event='read_admitted',conditions=[])],legality=legality),monitors=[dict(id='MON-forwarded-context',checker_id='CHK-forwarded-context',event='read_result',binding_ids=[binding],grounding=monitor_ground,admission_alias='admitted',applicability_conditions=[])],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='CHK-forwarded-context',kind='event_assertion',trigger=dict(field='event',op='eq',value='read_result'),assertion=dict(field='ctx',op='eq',reference='admitted.ctx'),identity_fields=['scenario','origin'],description='Exported readiness preserves the exact original SystemCtx for the independently identified originating operation.')],uncertainties=['No client RequestState deadline or application Lookup endpoint is executed; consequences beyond local response/readiness correlation remain unmeasured.', 'TestLogDB saves model crash-free persistence only; no statement about actual disk crash recovery.'])\nopen('read_context_plan.json','w').write(json.dumps(plan,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nsub=dict(action='check',rationale='Fix a narrow correlation check now that producer, consumer and independent test expectations establish the responsibility. Controlled overlap distinguishes per-status context routing from legitimate index coalescing; serial control checks the same route without prefix release.',sources=sources,candidate=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=candidate['id'],question=q,rationale='Ground the selected status-consumption responsibility without assuming a violation or any unconditional client deadline.',obligation=claim,bindings=[bind]),plan_path='read_context_plan.json',harness_path='read_context_test.go',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[candidate['id'],'M-read-prefix-test','M-read-receiver-test','M-read-client'],answered='The captured queue test requires each released status to preserve its own ctx/from despite index coalescing, and the receiver test requires message context to become readiness context. Exact client batch lookup explains why identity preservation is an applicable local responsibility. A fixed Peer driver now generates the overlapping history through Launch, Tick, ReadIndex and actual heartbeat/reply producers, with a sequential control and no protocol state mutation.',remaining=['Trusted execution must measure the fixed artifacts; semantic correspondence must assess actual observations and driver prerequisites.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='This establishes expectation and construction, not execution evidence. The narrower local correlation claim does not assert a timeout bound or linearizability consequence.'))\nopen('submission.json','w').write(json.dumps(sub,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python build_check.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_17-00-31-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
